R2 bidirectionality verification — Stage 8 / Phase 1 (interaction polish, ticket #37)
=====================================================================================

The R2 rule: every behavior this phase asserts must be shown to FAIL under a
targeted mutation of the implementation — a test that cannot fail proves nothing.
Each block below injects ONE mutant into the (committed) implementation, runs the
behavior's test(s) in isolation (`vitest run <file> -t "<name>"`), and records the
genuine FAIL. After each block the implementation is restored; the final suite is
GREEN (see the tail). Baseline test count before this phase: 575. After: 591
(+16). Mutants were applied to source only — the tests are exactly as committed.

Behaviors covered:
  B1  setStageMachineCount writes the NAMED non-active stage (mutant: writes active)
  B2  setStageMachineCount no-ops on an unknown id (mutant: drops the undefined guard)
  B3  setStageMachineCount(active) delegates + mirrors (mutant: drops mirrorActive)
  B4  apply block absent for over-supply (mutant: drops the under-supply type gate)
  B5/B5b fan-out payload wording "×N total" (mutant: hardcodes fanOut=false)
  B6/B6b unsolved producer → null suggestion (mutant: returns a bogus payload)
  B7/B7b single-consumer payload N = ceilDiv (mutant: machines+1 off-by-one)
  B8  matched link → null / idempotent presence (mutant: drops the finding gate)
  B9  active site renders the .selected outline (mutant: never applies the class)
  B10 site <g> button semantics role+tabIndex (mutant: drops them)
  B11 site click targets carry the exact stageIds (mutant: reverses site order)
  B12 idempotence via the finding gate — no under-supply once supply covers demand
      (mutant: reconcile emits under-supply even when supply>=demand)

